<body>

    <div class="cover-page">
        <h1>Hostel Desk Management Portal</h1>
        <p>Comprehensive Technical & Operational Documentation</p>
        <p><strong>Version:</strong> 2.0 (Updated 2026)</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Page Break -->
    <br clear="all" style="page-break-before:always" />

    <h2>1. Executive Summary</h2>
    <p>The <strong>Hostel Desk Management Portal</strong> is a secure, full-stack web application built on PHP and MySQL. It is designed to streamline facility operations and maintenance within university or corporate hostels. The system bridges the communication gap between residents and the operational team, ensuring that all maintenance requests are tracked, categorized, and resolved efficiently with a complete audit trail.</p>

    <h2>2. Key Features & Modules</h2>
    
    <h3>2.1. Student Portal (Maintenance Requests)</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Ticket Generation:</strong> Students can file detailed maintenance issues categorized by domain (e.g., Plumbing, Electrical, Wi-Fi).</li>
        <li><strong>Evidence Uploads:</strong> Support for attaching image evidence (JPG, PNG, WebP) with strict 5MB size and MIME type validation.</li>
        <li><strong>Live Tracking:</strong> Students can securely look up their ticket using a combination of the assigned Ticket ID and Room Number.</li>
        <li><strong>Ticket Timeline:</strong> View a chronological audit trail showing when a ticket was created and any status updates or comments provided by wardens.</li>
        <li><strong>1-Click Copy:</strong> Immediate feedback with a direct "Copy Ticket Number" capability post-submission.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>2.2. Warden Dashboard (Operations Center)</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Analytics Overview:</strong> Real-time key metrics showing Open, In Progress, and Resolved tickets, along with the most common issue category.</li>
        <li><strong>Actionable Modal Updates:</strong> A dedicated user interface for wardens to update ticket statuses. Every update requires an actionable comment to ensure transparency with the student.</li>
        <li><strong>Filter & Search:</strong> Powerful table filtering by status, priority, category, or direct search by name/room number.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>2.3. Platform Announcements (Notice Board)</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Warden Broadcasts:</strong> Wardens can publish hostel-wide notices (e.g., "Water supply disruption") with custom priority tags (Urgent, Maintenance, General).</li>
        <li><strong>Auto-Expiring Notices:</strong> Wardens define a specific `expires_at` date/time. Once passed, the notice automatically vanishes from the student dashboard.</li>
        <li><strong>Animated UI Banners:</strong> Active announcements are displayed dynamically on the student homepage featuring an animated megaphone to attract attention.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Security Architecture</h2>
    <p>Adhering to strict corporate security standards, the system employs multiple layers of defense:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Atomic Ticket Generation:</strong> Uses MySQL <code>SELECT ... FOR UPDATE</code> locks to guarantee gap-free ticket IDs (e.g., HC-2026-0001) even under heavy concurrent traffic.</li>
        <li><strong>Authentication:</strong> Staff accounts utilize PHP's robust <code>password_hash()</code> (Bcrypt) and secure HttpOnly session cookies.</li>
        <li><strong>Rate Limiting:</strong> Enforces an IP-based throttle limit (max 5 requests per hour) to prevent spamming the ticket submission endpoint.</li>
        <li><strong>Input Sanitization:</strong> Employs PDO Prepared Statements exclusively across all database interactions to nullify SQL Injection vulnerabilities.</li>
        <li><strong>Honeypot Anti-Bot:</strong> Implements a hidden honeypot field in the ticket submission form to trap automated bots.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Database Schema Overview</h2>
    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Table Name</th>
                <th>Purpose</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>wardens</strong></td>
                <td>Stores staff login credentials, Bcrypt password hashes, and active status.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>complaints</strong></td>
                <td>Core table tracking ticket details, priority, student info, room, and status.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>complaint_logs</strong></td>
                <td>Relational table capturing the audit trail of status changes and warden comments.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>announcements</strong></td>
                <td>Stores hostel-wide broadcasts, priority tags, and automated expiration timestamps.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>ticket_counters</strong></td>
                <td>High-performance locking table utilized to generate atomic, sequential ticket numbers.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>5. Deployment & Setup</h2>
    <p>To deploy the system on a new environment (XAMPP, LAMP, or production server), follow these steps:</p>
    <ol>
        <li>Import the core <code>database/schema.sql</code> file into the MySQL database to provision all required tables.</li>
        <li>Update <code>backend/db.php</code> with the target environment's database credentials.</li>
        <li>Ensure the <code>backend/uploads</code> directory has standard read/write permissions for the web server to process media uploads.</li>
        <li>Execute a script to generate the first administrative Warden account, as the system does not seed default weak passwords.</li>
    </ol>
    <p><strong>End of Document.</strong></p>
</body>
